# NOTE FOR THE MAINTAINER
# 1. After tagging release v1.0.1 (which contains the corrected cRp2 calculation),
#    update "version", "date-released" and "doi" below with the version-specific
#    Zenodo DOI of that release, not the concept DOI.
# 2. Fill in the two missing ORCID identifiers.
# 3. Once the Application Note is published, uncomment the "preferred-citation"
#    block at the end and complete it. GitHub's "Cite this repository" button
#    will then offer the article instead of the software record.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KhemSAR in your research, please cite both the software (below) and the accompanying article."
title: "KhemSAR: An Open-Source Platform for OECD-Aligned QSAR Validation, Mechanistic SAR Interpretation and Bioisosteric De Novo Design"
type: software
version: "1.0.1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24318136"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sbolivar16/KhemSAR"
url: "https://github.com/Sbolivar16/KhemSAR"
authors:
  - family-names: "Bolívar Ávila"
    given-names: "Santiago"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3772-7604"
    affiliation: "Master's Programme in Biotechnology, Universidad Libre, Puerto Colombia 080007, Colombia"
  - family-names: "Navarro"
    given-names: "Richard"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"
    affiliation: "Universidad del Atlántico, Facultad de Ciencias Básicas, Departamento de Química, Puerto Colombia, Atlántico, Colombia"
  - family-names: "España Puccini"
    given-names: "Pierine"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"
    affiliation: "IMB-Research Group in Medicine and Biotechnology, Universidad Libre, Puerto Colombia 080007, Colombia"
keywords:
  - QSAR
  - SAR
  - cheminformatics
  - drug discovery
  - bioisosterism
  - de novo design
  - applicability domain
  - OECD principles
  - matched molecular pairs
  - model validation
abstract: >-
  KhemSAR is a cross-platform (macOS, Linux, Windows), multilingual (English, Spanish,
  Portuguese), MIT-licensed scientific platform that unifies retrieval from ten open
  chemical resources, deterministic chemical structure curation, QSAR validation aligned
  with the five OECD principles, mechanistic structure-activity interpretation through
  activity cliffs, matched molecular pairs and feature attribution, bioisosteric de novo
  design with three-dimensional ligand and receptor preparation, and a context-aware
  scientific tutoring layer. Every run writes an auditable workspace.

